# What every project ignores, whatever it is built in: the droppings an editor and an
# operating system leave beside your work. No language, no framework, no cloud — those
# would be a guess at what this project is, and `git add -A` runs before anyone knows.
#
# `kit init --stack <name>` writes that stack's file in place of this one.

# macOS
.DS_Store
._*

# Windows
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Linux
.directory
.Trash-*

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Merge and patch leftovers
*.orig
*.rej

# Secrets — kit commits with `git add -A` on pause and harvest, so a local env file must
# never be addable. The committed template stays.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
